Namaste Friend! Ek dynamic portfolio tracker banana ek bahut hi behtareen project hai. Isme hum HTML, CSS aur JavaScript ka use karenge aur chart ke liye **Chart.js** library ka istemal karenge jo ki bahut lightweight aur powerful hai.

Niche ek complete, production-ready structure diya gaya hai.

### Project Structure:
1.  **index.html**: UI layout.
2.  **style.css**: Modern styling.
3.  **script.js**: Logic, Balance calculation aur Chart rendering.

---

### 1. `index.html`
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Portfolio Tracker</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>My Portfolio Tracker</h1>
        <div class="balance-card">
            <h3>Total Balance: ₹<span id="total-balance">0</span></h3>
        </div>

        <div class="input-section">
            <input type="text" id="asset-name" placeholder="Asset Name (e.g., AAPL)">
            <input type="number" id="asset-value" placeholder="Value (₹)">
            <button onclick="addAsset()">Add Asset</button>
        </div>

        <canvas id="portfolioChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 2. `style.css`
```css
body { font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif; background: #f4f7f6; padding: 20px; }
.container { max-width: 600px; margin: auto; background: white; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); }
.balance-card { background: #2c3e50; color: white; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.input-section { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
input { padding: 10px; flex: 1; }
button { padding: 10px 20px; background: #27ae60; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
```

---

### 3. `script.js`
```javascript
let portfolioData = {
    labels: [],
    values: []
};

const ctx = document.getElementById('portfolioChart').getContext('2d');
const myChart = new Chart(ctx, {
    type: 'pie',
    data: {
        labels: portfolioData.labels,
        datasets: [{
            data: portfolioData.values,
            backgroundColor: ['#FF6384', '#36A2EB', '#FFCE56', '#4BC0C0']
        }]
    }
});

function addAsset() {
    const name = document.getElementById('asset-name').value;
    const value = parseFloat(document.getElementById('asset-value').value);

    if (name && value) {
        portfolioData.labels.push(name);
        portfolioData.values.push(value);

        updateUI();
    }
}

function updateUI() {
    // Update Balance
    const total = portfolioData.values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
    document.getElementById('total-balance').innerText = total.toFixed(2);

    // Update Chart
    myChart.update();
}
```

### Kaise chalayein:
1. Teeno files ko ek folder mein save karein.
2. `index.html` ko apne browser mein open karein.
3. Asset ka naam aur value daalein, aur "Add Asset" button par click karein.

**Pro Tip:** Kyunki aapne financial data analysis mein interest dikhaya hai, agle step mein hum isme `fetch` API ka use karke real-time stock prices (jaise Yahoo Finance ya Alpha Vantage API) integrate kar sakte hain.

